{%- comment -%}
  Self-hosted fonts, served from Shopify's CDN alongside the rest of the theme.

  This replaces a Google Fonts <link>, which was a render-blocking request to a
  third party on every page load - and is blocked outright in some countries,
  where it would have silently dropped the store to a system font.

  Inter is the variable file, so ONE download covers 300 through 700. Declaring
  the axis range on a single @font-face is what makes that work; listing the
  weights separately would fetch the same file five times.

  Both faces are SIL Open Font License, which permits self-hosting.

  theme-check suggests the preload_tag filter here. These are written out by
  hand on purpose: a font preload MUST carry crossorigin, and if it does not
  match the crossorigin of the actual @font-face fetch the browser downloads
  the file twice - slower than not preloading at all. Explicit tags make that
  attribute impossible to lose.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'inter.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'anton.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
<style>
  @font-face{
    font-family:'Inter';
    font-style:normal;
    font-weight:100 900;
    font-display:swap;
    src:url({{ 'inter.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
  }
  @font-face{
    font-family:'Anton';
    font-style:normal;
    font-weight:400;
    font-display:swap;
    src:url({{ 'anton.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
  }
</style>
